WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:02.966
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.966 --> 00:00:06.233
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.866 --> 00:00:11.600
- Hi, I'm Alexandra Billings,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.400
and I'll be reading an
excerpt from my upcoming book,

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.366
This Time for Me.

00:00:19.366 --> 00:00:21.933
Early one morning, as the
sun streaked across the tile

00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:23.800
of our newly laid kitchen floor,

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.066
I sat cross-legged in one of
Mimi's long green dresses,

00:00:28.066 --> 00:00:30.933
barefoot, and eating my Frosted Flakes

00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:32.500
directly from the box,

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.233
looking out into our backyard.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.133
I had only put on lipstick
that morning, no other makeup.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:42.200
I was six and had been dressing
up for a while by then.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.533
It seemed a part of me.

00:00:45.533 --> 00:00:48.166
I felt better.

00:00:48.166 --> 00:00:49.000
I was happy.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.200
My feet clicked as I wobbled
back and forth on the floor.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.866
My long dress covering my knees

00:00:54.866 --> 00:00:56.300
and my lipstick smearing a bit

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.200
as the flakes spilled out onto my lap

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.266
and stuck to my cheeks.

00:01:00.266 --> 00:01:02.366
I began to hum We've Only Just Begun,

00:01:02.366 --> 00:01:03.800
which was my theme song.

00:01:04.666 --> 00:01:06.133
I was humming,

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:08.666
playing with a beam of
light in the early morning,

00:01:08.666 --> 00:01:10.466
and picking up random flakes

00:01:10.466 --> 00:01:13.500
from both my lap and our
spotless kitchen floor.

00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:16.733
I had found my joy.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.833
As Mimi turned the corner

00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:22.966
from the dining room into the kitchen,

00:01:22.966 --> 00:01:24.833
I felt my heart race.

00:01:24.833 --> 00:01:27.833
I knew the mess on the floor
and on me might set her off.

00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:29.966
I began to clean up as quickly as I could.

00:01:29.966 --> 00:01:32.033
I was singing a song she loved

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:34.600
and I hoped she might wanna join me.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.033
She'd never really heard me sing.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:38.100
And I was having such a good time

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.133
I thought she might
want to come and join me

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.333
for my Karen Carpenter
Frosted Flakes party.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.800
She stopped as I turned towards her,

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.600
my back to the sliding glass doors.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.933
Her face dropped and
her eyes began to lower.

00:01:53.366 --> 00:01:54.200
I thought at first

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.600
she was staring at the
crumbs on the floor,

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.900
and then I realized she
was staring at the dress.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.933
Her head began to shake. Her
mouth turned downward a little.

00:02:02.933 --> 00:02:05.666
And I felt my insides begin to churn

00:02:05.666 --> 00:02:07.633
as if I had eaten bad cheese.

00:02:09.066 --> 00:02:11.966
She didn't speak or move.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.433
And then in a whisper,

00:02:15.433 --> 00:02:17.600
she said methodically
and with great emphasis,

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.900
"Don't ever wear that again."

00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:24.566
I held my breath.

00:02:24.566 --> 00:02:25.400
"Scott,

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.266
do you understand me?" she asked.

00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:33.700
Her eyes flashed black

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.966
and her finger pointed
at my borrowed gown.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.266
From all of us to all of you

00:02:43.266 --> 00:02:46.033
with great love and many blessings,

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.133
Happy Transgender Awareness Week.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.566
Thank you.

00:02:50.566 --> 00:02:54.300
(upbeat music and applause)

